    {
      "id": "b000018",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 53,
      "end_line": 53,
      "raw": "## Notes\n",
      "level": 2,
      "title": "Notes"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000019",
      "kind": "list",
      "start_line": 54,
      "end_line": 66,
      "raw": "- `LibraryNoteRecord` now exposes structural equality so incremental mutation layers can suppress no-op updates before\n  they fan out into note-list/calendar rebuilds.\n- `LibraryAll`, `LibraryDraft`, and `LibraryToday` now all support single-note upsert/remove operations, and\n  `WhatSonLibraryIndexedState` uses those paths to keep canonical and derived buckets synchronized without replacing\n  the whole note snapshot on every local edit.\n- `LibraryNotePreviewText.hpp` is the shared preview-text authority for library note cards and calendar note chips, so\n  compact note renderers do not drift into separate headline rules.\n- `LibraryHierarchyController` owns the hub-independent in-app scaffold (`All Library`, `Drafts`, `Today`) and must keep\n  it visible during construction, empty depth refreshes, runtime snapshot refreshes, and load-failure recovery.\n- `LibraryHierarchyModel.hpp` is now an item-struct/icon-helper header. The runtime item model exposed to QML is the\n  shared `WhatSonHierarchyModel` owned by the controller.\n- `WhatSonLibraryNoteListProjection` mirrors that scaffold label contract by using `Drafts` for notes that have no\n  explicit hub-authored folder chips.\n",
      "items": [
